description: Inline React Query mutation/query keys; no key factory helpers
alwaysApply: true
---

# React Query keys

Always write keys inline as arrays. Export only the base string constant if needed. Do not create helper functions that return `[KEY, id] as const`.

```ts
// BAD
export function workoutWriteMutationKey(workoutId: string) {
  return [WORKOUT_WRITE_MUTATION_KEY, workoutId] as const;
}
mutationKey: workoutWriteMutationKey(workoutId)

// GOOD
export const WORKOUT_WRITE_MUTATION_KEY = "workout-write";
mutationKey: [WORKOUT_WRITE_MUTATION_KEY, workoutId]
queryKey: [WORKOUT_DETAILS_QUERY_KEY, workoutId]
```

Same for `useIsMutating`, `invalidateQueries`, and anywhere else a key is passed.
